139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 114 0 R
/T (The Why I Love Myself \(WILM\) project is dedicated to empowering young girls and gender nonbinary individuals by fostering self-worth, resilience, and confidence during their formative middle school years. WILM seeks to create a supportive environment where students can explore and embrace their unique identities. Led by college students from CU Boulder, this initiative is also centered around mentorship, allowing students to connect with relatable role models to guide them through practical strategies in self-love, body positivity, friendship skills, speaking skills, and personal growth. By building a strong foundation of self-esteem and offering a community of encouragement, WILM aims to positively impact their mental health and emotional well-being, inspiring them to grow into confident, empowered individuals. . Through twice monthly workshops at the Girls Athletic Leadership School \(GALS\), the project will focus on fostering self-love, body positivity, empowerment, public speaking, friendship skills, healthy habits, and resilience. Each workshop is designed to equip young girls with practical strategies to navigate the pressures they face and be able to manage them while also encouraging empowerment and personal growth. )
/E (The Why I Love Myself \(WILM\) project is dedicated to empowering young girls and gender nonbinary individuals by fostering self-worth, resilience, and confidence during their formative middle school years. WILM seeks to create a supportive environment where students can explore and embrace their unique identities. Led by college students from CU Boulder, this initiative is also centered around mentorship, allowing students to connect with relatable role models to guide them through practical strategies in self-love, body positivity, friendship skills, speaking skills, and personal growth. By building a strong foundation of self-esteem and offering a community of encouragement, WILM aims to positively impact their mental health and emotional well-being, inspiring them to grow into confident, empowered individuals. . Through twice monthly workshops at the Girls Athletic Leadership School \(GALS\), the project will focus on fostering self-love, body positivity, empowerment, public speaking, friendship skills, healthy habits, and resilience. Each workshop is designed to equip young girls with practical strategies to navigate the pressures they face and be able to manage them while also encouraging empowerment and personal growth. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
